DTSTAMP:20261107T161641Z
DTSTART;VALUE=DATE:20261107
DTEND;VALUE=DATE:20261108
SUMMARY:Run Friends Run 5k & Pet-Friendly Fun Run
DESCRIPTION:Run Friends Run 5k is a race through the beautiful 54-acre campus of Friends Meeting School (FMS) and the surrounding neighborhood. The chip-timed 5k is part cross-country (on campus) and part road race. The pet-friendly\, 1-mile\, untimed\, fun run takes place on campus. Coordinated by FMS parent volunteers\, this event celebrates the benefits of physical exercise and community\, and it raises money to support the school’s academic programs and staff.
URL:https://www.visitfrederick.org/event/run-friends-run-5k-%26-pet-friendly-fun-run/26066/
END:VEVENT
BEGIN:VEVENT
UID:httpswwwvisitfrederickorgeventsourdoughbreadbakingclass24405-20261107@visitfrederick
DTSTAMP:20261107T161641Z
DTSTART;VALUE=DATE:20261107
DTEND;VALUE=DATE:20261108
SUMMARY:Sourdough Bread Baking Class
DESCRIPTION:Join Frederick home bakers Jon & Emily for a sourdough bread baking class designed for beginner bakers! Slow-fermented sourdough bread is beloved for its digestibility (especially for those of us with gluten sensitivity)\, lower glycemic index\, and its keeping power without preservatives. Its complex\, delicious flavor and airy\, chewy texture cannot be beat! Beyond the joys of eating sourdough bread\, many also enjoy the therapeutic nature of a slow\, mindful hobby that doubles as a satisfying creative outlet. It's a science experiment you get to eat! In this 2-hour class\, we will practice mixing\, shaping\, and baking a traditional sourdough bâtard (an oval-shaped loaf). You will leave class with: • your own sourdough starter (+ feeding instructions) • banneton proofing basket + cloth liner + bench scraper • a shaped dough to bake at home the same afternoon as class • a bonus dough to practice another shape & bake at home • printed and PDF versions of the recipe and instructions taught in class • support from your new sourdough bread baking friends!
URL:https://www.visitfrederick.org/event/sourdough-bread-baking-class/24405/
END:VEVENT
BEGIN:VEVENT
UID:httpswwwvisitfrederickorgeventthe19thstreetbandlive26271-20261107@visitfrederick
DTSTAMP:20261107T161641Z
DTSTART;VALUE=DATE:20261107
DTEND;VALUE=DATE:20261108
SUMMARY:The 19th Street Band Live
DESCRIPTION:The 19th Street Band LIVE in Concert at Rockwell Brewery with the Back Alley Horns!! Don't miss out on your chance to catch The 19th Street Band live in FREDERICK on Saturday\, Nov 7th with their very own horn section! Always a fun\, rockin'\, good time band\, these folks will have you energized all night long!!! This time\, they are offering four preferred seating areas for groups of 5-6. Check out the ticket tiers to guarantee your seating for the night. Otherwise\, General Admission is available for all who plan to dance the night away! The Show starts at 8PM. Pro Tip - Get here early to grab a prime seat near the stage! We can’t wait for this Saturday Night party!
URL:https://www.visitfrederick.org/event/the-19th-street-band-live/26271/
END:VEVENT
BEGIN:VEVENT
UID:httpswwwvisitfrederickorgevent94thannualbrunswickveteransday11531-20261108@visitfrederick
DTSTAMP:20261107T161641Z
DTSTART;VALUE=DATE:20261108
DTEND;VALUE=DATE:20261109
SUMMARY:94th Annual Brunswick Veterans Day 
DESCRIPTION:Join the Brunswick community on Sunday\, November 8\, 2026\, for our annual Veterans Day Parade\, a meaningful tradition honoring those who have served our nation. This year’s event will also recognize America’s 250th Anniversary\, adding special significance to the day. The celebration will begin with an Opening Ceremony at 1:00 PM\, followed by the Veterans Day Parade stepping off at 2:00 PM. Community members are invited to line the parade route and take part in this tribute of gratitude\, remembrance\, and patriotism.
URL:https://www.visitfrederick.org/event/94th-annual-brunswick-veterans-day/11531/
END:VEVENT
BEGIN:VEVENT
UID:httpswwwvisitfrederickorgeventcelebrating40yearsofwinemakinginfrederickcounty26264-20261108@visitfrederick
DTSTAMP:20261107T161641Z
DTSTART;VALUE=DATE:20261108
DTEND;VALUE=DATE:20261109
SUMMARY:Celebrating 40 Years of Wine Making in Frederick County
DESCRIPTION:Frederick County is home to three of Maryland's oldest wineries\, each with a legacy dating back to the 1970s and 1980s. Join the families behind Elk Run Vineyards\, Loew Vineyards\, and Linganore Winecellars for an afternoon of conversation. Together\, they'll reflect on 50 years of grape growing and winemaking in Frederick County\, sharing the stories that shaped Maryland's wine industry. Hear firsthand about the triumphs\, challenges\, innovations\, and unexpected moments of collaboration that have defined these pioneering wineries. Hosted by Melissa Aellen\, Director of Winery Operations for Linganore.
URL:https://www.visitfrederick.org/event/celebrating-40-years-of-wine-making-in-frederick-county/26264/
END:VEVENT
